{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "במי", :translit "ba'may", :gloss "in waters of"} {:he "במי הנדה", :translit "ba'may ha'nidah", :gloss "in the waters of the menstruant"} {:he "אך במי נדה יתחטא", :translit "akh ba'may nidah yit'chata", :gloss "only in waters of nidah shall he be cleansed"} {:he "במי מריבת קדש", :translit "ba'may merivat kodesh", :gloss "in the waters of Merivat Kadesh"} {:he "במי הירדן", :translit "ba'may ha'yarden", :gloss "in the waters of the Jordan"} {:he "אם התרחצתי במי שלג", :translit "im hit'rachatzti ba'may sheleg", :gloss "if I have washed in waters of snow"} {:he "ויאמר אלעזר הכהן אל אנשי הצבא", :translit "va'yomer el'azar ha'kohen el anshei ha'tzava", :gloss "and Elazar the priest said to the men of the army"} {:he "גיעול", :translit "gi'ul", :gloss "purging of vessels"} {:he "מריבה", :translit "merivah", :gloss "strife"} {:he "נדה", :translit "nidah", :gloss "menstruant"} {:he "זחילה", :translit "z'chilah", :gloss "crawling/flowing"} {:he "שלג", :translit "sheleg", :gloss "snow"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 5, :occurrences ["במי הנדה" "אך במי נדה יתחטא" "במי מריבת קדש" "במי הירדן" "אם התרחצתי במי שלג"]}], :frame {:text "Five verses contain the phrase במי and the Masorah lists them together. The phrase במי מריבת קדש in Numbers 20:13 links to Numbers 31:21, where Elazar instructs the soldiers after the war with Midian. The tradition that Moses became angry and thereby forgot to teach the laws of purging captured vessels is found in the Sifrei on Numbers 31:21. The requirement that a mikveh contain forty se'ah is stated in Mishnah Mikva'ot 7:1. Shmuel's prohibition against immersing in rivers, lest dripping water increase upon flowing water and fail to purify through contact, appears in Shabbat 65b. The testimony of the men of Meidba that Rabbi Yishma'el permitted making a mikveh from snow at the outset is recorded in Mishnah Mikva'ot 7:1.", :sources ["Numbers 20:13" "Numbers 31:21" "Sifrei Numbers 157" "Mish